{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm","id":1265809,"title":"Fates of Canon NPCs experiencing Avatar Storm ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-09T07:12:17-08:00","id":1265809,"title":"Fates of Canon NPCs experiencing Avatar Storm ?","content":"Uh , so we all know Avatar Storm causes serious effects , many powerful elders in Mage society can't return (And to my surprise , this is even mentioned in a Hunter Enemy Book ! ) So what do you know about that Canon NPC's fate after this disaster ? Or you can share your idea about this ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:23:57-08:00","id":1265815,"title":"","content":"The vast majority of Technocrats got incorporated into Threat Null.<br /> <br /> Tradition mages are less warped, but still got Disembodied and are nothing but Spirits mindlessly repeating the actions of their old lives. Archmasters of Spirit/DimSci might be an exception, since to become one you <i>have</i> to become Disembodied and then turn yoursefl into a human again, per <i>Masters of the Art</i>.<br /> <br /> Senex and Voormas survived, but Voormas may not be around any more judging by the extended timeline of M20, which is kinda reliant on his plan failing totally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-09-2018, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:38:37-08:00","id":1265817,"title":"","content":"Is there a list of Canon NPCs who are destroyed or trapped in Avatar Storm ? I want to know some powerful NPC's fate ... like those guys in Book of Chantries ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T07:46:12-08:00","id":1265820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265817#post1265817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a list of Canon NPCs who are destroyed or trapped in Avatar Storm ? I want to know some powerful NPC's fate ... like those guys in Book of Chantries ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think <i>The Infinite Tapestry</i> has some info on Realms that were destroyed by the Storm, so it might be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T08:23:08-08:00","id":1265831,"title":"","content":"Doissetep mages got blown up with their Chantry before the Storm.<br /> <br /> MECHA was lost, and while it's fate it's unknown I think it's higly likely that the Construct it's part of Threat Null now. I doub't the Matriarch it's human enough to exist in Earth without help, and without Earthly Nodes providing protection against Void Adaptation she should have lost the little humanity she had.<br /> <br /> Of other luminaries, Doc Eon fate it's unknown but his Acolites trust he will survive (and he does appear in the fiction of ToJ: Ascencion, so there's that.)<br /> <br /> Senex has a bunch of refugees in Charon, Gilmore among them (not sure if others get mentioned)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T10:17:37-08:00","id":1265862,"title":"","content":"Porthos becomes the Oracle of Forces and saves the world from the Conflagration<br /> <br /> Marianna becomes the Oracle of Time<br /> <br /> Archmaster Gentle Mountain dies when he get through the gauntlet and is shredded by the avatar storm; he came back to leave his legacy to Raging Eagle, now a Sifu of the Kannagara.<br /> <br /> Cristavao gets killed by the Ascension warrior, his death starts the Conflagration of Doissetep<br /> <br /> Lord Gilmore survives the cataclysm and seals Horizon before the collapse; he becomes Primus of House Tytalus and lead them after the worst of the Massasa War<br /> <br /> Senex calls back Euthanatos to India; Euthanatos must abbandon their daily strife and struggles to join him in a great project to use Voormas ritual to cleanse the Wheel from the excess of entropy. Only by abbandoning earth they can save the Tellurian.<br /> <br /> Theora becomes the herald of Senex.<br /> <br /> The house of Helekar is wiped out; member after member they fall at the hands of the assassin sent by the Traditions. Only Voormas survive, taking shelter in Yomi Wan, as a honoured guest of the Yama King Thou Mou, out of the reach of the Traditions. It is hinted that Voormas, now the most powerful archmage in existence, is the author of the awakening of Ravnos in India and is the mastermind behind the Avatar storm. The house itself travels through reality, last time it has been spotted in northern Poland.<br /> <br /> Alex Hastings becomes the Oracle of Matter<br /> <br /> Ihuanocuatlo of the Dreamspeakers and leader of Vali Shalar becomes the Oracle of Spirit<br /> <br /> Marianna of Balador, who shares the same avatar of Akrites, becomes the Oracle of Time<br /> <br /> Nightshade becomes the Oracle of Life<br /> <br /> Caeron Mustai...this is a hell of a ride...Caeron Mustai is killed by Porthos at Doissetep, then resurrected by Oracle Porthos and the Phoenix, who choose him as a new champion for Ascension. Mustai decide to repent and paving the way for Ascension, is first act is joining the Vrati of the Euthanatos, under the guise of &quot;Iago&quot; and leads the purge of the old House Janissary, preventing them from betraying the Traditions. After the purge he becomes one of the main agent of the Rogue Council, while keeping is role as the leader of the Vrati.<br /> <br /> Every mage in at Victoria Station becomes a spirit.<br /> <br /> Every Technocrat who is left behind in the Umbra becomes a member of Threat Null.<br /> <br /> The Jade Demon survives the storm and is currently the only Akashic Archmage who has contact with Earth.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T10:42:19-08:00","id":1265867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every Technocrat who is left behind in the Umbra becomes a member of Threat Null.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's heavily implied to be the case for most, but the fate of Void Engineers it's unknown. They just vanished, albeit some voidships were seen coming out from the old COP (now a black hole).<br /> <br /> Being the only Technocrats that make a heavy use of DimSci (which includes ways to prevent Void Adaptation at level 5), the ones that knew what would happen after 3 months in deep universe, this is higly suspicious.<br /> Theories:<br /> <br /> *They sucumbed to Void Adaptation but weren't assimilated into Threat Null because that force has it's foundation on Social Conditioning, and the VE routinely break Social Conditioning and replace it with their own. So they've become an independant force, probably akin to the Grays, trough LERMU-ization.<br /> <br /> *They're a faction of Treath Null that's yet to be revealed, perhaps even the masterminds behind the force. Seeing what would happen they could have embraced Disembodiment and made an active effort to take control of the nascent force - something plausible because everyone it's an EDE now and they're the ones who have the Sphere that controls EDEs.<br /> <br /> *Some managed to survive but they're hiding in another universe. This one it's unlikely because they should have tried to comunicate, but not impossible if the universe it's remote enough (Say, perhaps in a different Everet Volume).<br /> <br /> Moon Base fell to the forces that were already attacking it (spirits and fae-like beings, if I remember correctly) soon after the storm, so it's possible that it's members just died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-09-2018, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T10:45:16-08:00","id":1265869,"title":"","content":"Ah yeah, sorry, that's true, Void Engineers have not been spotted among Threat Null.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T11:36:56-08:00","id":1265880,"title":"","content":"That is broadly correct but IIRC the stuff about the Council members becoming Oracles (and the fate of Caeron Mustai) is from the now-noncanon <i>Ascension</i> scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T15:59:04-08:00","id":1265955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265880#post1265880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is broadly correct but IIRC the stuff about the Council members becoming Oracles (and the fate of Caeron Mustai) is from the now-noncanon <i>Ascension</i> scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember those are from the Ascension Appendix ? ... I remember this is just a optional stuff , not canon , other Endings in Chapters may differ from it ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-09-2018, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:01:56-08:00","id":1265958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265862#post1265862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Jade Demon survives the storm and is currently the only Akashic Archmage who has contact with Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember he is a Akashic barrabi... does he join the Tradition later ? let me check it ...<br /> And , how much update in Book of Chantries later ? In my opinion many very old or powerful mages should be updated to Archmages ... ( Ihuanocuatlo and Jade Demon and Mustai may be so , and I think Glarius in Sea of Ash may follow ? Too many ...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-09-2018, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:05:47-08:00","id":1265962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265955#post1265955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember those are from the Ascension Appendix ? ... I remember this is just a optional stuff , not canon , other Endings in Chapters may differ from it ...</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 5 separate scenarios in Ascension, none of which are canon anymore - &quot;Ascension&quot; used to be the canon ending but now the whole Time of Judgement has been retconned/took place in an alternate universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-09T16:17:23-08:00","id":1265969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265962#post1265962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are 5 separate scenarios in Ascension, none of which are canon anymore - &quot;Ascension&quot; used to be the canon ending but now the whole Time of Judgement has been retconned/took place in an alternate universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know , you can choose the Ending you want . It's up to you . All ToJ books like this .<br /> And , uh , I remember Introduction in \u300aAscension \u300bsays that Chapter Ascension is just an optional Ending which is more &quot;official&quot; , not canon .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-10-2018, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:36:04-08:00","id":1266528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1265969#post1265969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know , you can choose the Ending you want . It's up to you . All ToJ books like this .<br /> And , uh , I remember Introduction in \u300aAscension \u300bsays that Chapter Ascension is just an optional Ending which is more &quot;official&quot; , not canon .</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it was the only one of them written as an official ending to the metaplot and the line. The other ones just don't make that much sense and only work on their own, not as an actual part of the metaplot.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T16:42:33-08:00","id":1266534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266528#post1266528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but it was the only one of them written as an official ending to the metaplot and the line. The other ones just don't make that much sense and only work on their own, not as an actual part of the metaplot.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that it had a dedicated novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-11T22:24:49-08:00","id":1266611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266528#post1266528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but it was the only one of them written as an official ending to the metaplot and the line. The other ones just don't make that much sense and only work on their own, not as an actual part of the metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266534#post1266534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that it had a dedicated novel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh , but why WhiteWolf did this ? ... Don't kick me , I always think &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; is more official (Although it is not that &quot;real&quot; because it's the worst condition you can imagine ... )<br /> <br /> PS : Do other Series in ToJ have &quot;more official&quot; Ending like this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-12-2018, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T00:00:55-08:00","id":1266626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266611#post1266611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh ... Where mentioned this ? M20 reconnects 6th Malestorm ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the world didn't end in 2004 and the Red Star disappeared soon after showing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1410,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","user":"Czernobog","date":". 11-12-2018, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T00:26:56-08:00","id":1266627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266626#post1266626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the world didn't end in 2004 and the Red Star disappeared soon after showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks . I expect more 5E books ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:03:34-08:00","id":1266646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266611#post1266611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh , but why WhiteWolf did this ? ... Don't kick me , I always think &quot;Hell on Earth&quot; is more official (Although it is not that &quot;real&quot; because it's the worst condition you can imagine ... )<br /> <br /> PS : Do other Series in ToJ have &quot;more official&quot; Ending like this ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? It was kind of the same with Wraith's Ends of Empire, even if that one wasn't ToJ.<br /> <br /> Also Hell on Earth is bad, the players can't do anything but to see the events unfold without any leeway and brought back a mostly forgotten character from Book of Madness 1st Edition to be an unstoppable villain sue without any kind of nuance. It also ignored the narrative going on at the moment for the sake of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266626#post1266626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the world didn't end in 2004 and the Red Star disappeared soon after showing up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't the Red Star still going on in the Beckett Jyhad Diary? I don't remember if there was any mention in Mage, but it's so toolbox-like with metaplot that I don't think that it would give an outright answer anyway. The Avatar Storm was kind of there, just weaker and more random.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 11-12-2018, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:30:24-08:00","id":1266654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266646#post1266646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? It was kind of the same with Wraith's Ends of Empire, even if that one wasn't ToJ.<br /> <br /> Also Hell on Earth is bad, the players can't do anything but to see the events unfold without any leeway and brought back a mostly forgotten character from Book of Madness 1st Edition to be an unstoppable villain sue without any kind of nuance. It also ignored the narrative going on at the moment for the sake of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's a choice between ...<br /> <br /> *railroading PCs between talking heads who exposit on the metaplot and deliver plot coupons, all the way to the final battle with Voormas<br /> *a scenario that doesn't even include <i>any</i> clues on how to incorporate the PCs, apparently<br /> *an <i>Armageddon-</i>esque scenario where all the factions' attempts to stop a meteorite end up interfering with each other, but the PCs <i>might</i> save a tiny fraction of humanity<br /> *aliens stealing Avatars, who have to be rescued from their spaceship<br /> *PCs get to watch as a Villain Sue kills everybody and turns the setting into a post-apocalyptic nightmare<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wasn't the Red Star still going on in the Beckett Jyhad Diary? I don't remember if there was any mention in Mage, but it's so toolbox-like with metaplot that I don't think that it would give an outright answer anyway. The Avatar Storm was kind of there, just weaker and more random. </div> </div> </div>According to the Wiki:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett&#39;s_Jyhad_Diary\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett's_Jyhad_Diary</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li>The <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Red_Star\" target=\"_blank\">Red Star</a> appeared and vanished.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>And ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Convention Book: Void Engineers</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Fifteen years ago, 28978 Ixion puzzled astronomers by exhibiting the characteristics of a redshifted microstar. NSC agents have spent a decade eliminating evidence of this \u201cRed Star event\u201d for a number of reasons, the most important of which is that we still have no goddamn idea what it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T03:48:41-08:00","id":1266659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266654#post1266654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it's a choice between ...<br /> <br /> *railroading PCs between talking heads who exposit on the metaplot and deliver plot coupons, all the way to the final battle with Voormas<br /> *a scenario that doesn't even include <i>any</i> clues on how to incorporate the PCs, apparently<br /> *an <i>Armageddon-</i>esque scenario where all the factions' attempts to stop a meteorite end up interfering with each other, but the PCs <i>might</i> save a tiny fraction of humanity<br /> *aliens stealing Avatars, who have to be rescued from their spaceship<br /> *PCs get to watch as a Villain Sue kills everybody and turns the setting into a post-apocalyptic nightmare</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree that Judgment it's that much of a railroad, as it has a lot of space between events to do a lot of other stuff if you want (or tackle things the scenario just tangentially touches) and the players are actually doing something and being the center of the action. You are right about the plot coupons though. Add the thing about being obtuse to players that don't know the metaplot.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266654#post1266654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the Wiki:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett&#39;s_Jyhad_Diary\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett's_Jyhad_Diary</a><br /> <br /> <br /> And ...</div> </div> </div> </div>I read Beckett's Jyhad Diary and I'm pretty sure they mention the star is still there more than once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","user":"History","date":". 11-12-2018, 06:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-12T16:14:22-08:00","id":1266809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>History</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266646#post1266646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Hell on Earth is bad, the players can't do anything but to see the events unfold without any leeway and brought back a mostly forgotten character from Book of Madness 1st Edition to be an unstoppable villain sue without any kind of nuance. It also ignored the narrative going on at the moment for the sake of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah , it is unreasonable , &quot; Bad guys never lost &quot; . There is no any other thing except tragedy in this Chapter ...And bringing back a NPC who is only mentioned 10 years ago is not a good idea ... <br /> <br /> I'm wrong , the reason why this Chapter leaves me the most impression is that it has many Very Badass Guys (Aswadims , thousands of years old )... &quot;Broaden my knowledge&quot; ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 11-16-2018, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T06:25:37-08:00","id":1267820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1266809#post1266809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wrong , the reason why this Chapter leaves me the most impression is that it has many Very Badass Guys (Aswadims , thousands of years old )... &quot;Broaden my knowledge&quot; ... At least there is no such mages before (Dead Magic ll has a Etrurian mage , that's the only exception I remember...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Voormas or even Aleph are better villains without the need of them being thousands of years old.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T08:46:21-08:00","id":1267857,"title":"","content":"Ascension was a pretty bad book that missed the point of Mage. &quot;The End Times are Upon us&quot; was never really a major theme of Mage, and just forcing random apocalypses on players is not the way to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-17T09:39:10-08:00","id":1268302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1267857#post1267857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ascension was a pretty bad book that missed the point of Mage. &quot;The End Times are Upon us&quot; was never really a major theme of Mage, and just forcing random apocalypses on players is not the way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the line was ending and it was a editorial plot point for all lines so at the time it had to happen one way or another.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1830-history","name":"History","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T20:35:01-08:00","id":1355330,"title":"","content":"I always felt there were more plot contrivances involved in getting Voormas to his apocalypse than in the Hell on Earth scenario. At least in that one it was pretty much a unified effort by the Nephandi and their masters, and the Aswadim had been laying the groundwork for it for milennia rather than one centuries-old necromancer suddenly getting his hands on a macguffin that let him reshape the universe.<br /> <br /> In light of books that have come out since the Book of Chantries, I'd probably classify the Jade Demon as a Wu Lung <i>barrabus</i> rather than Akashic. Though I suppose it doesn't matter much, as he was probably one of the <i>Gall</i><i>\u00fb</i> for hundreds of years before the Gilledeans came along and he joined their number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T03:49:23-08:00","id":1355355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1355330#post1355330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always felt there were more plot contrivances involved in getting Voormas to his apocalypse than in the Hell on Earth scenario.<br /> <br /> In light of books that have come out since the Book of Chantries,</div> </div> </div> </div>I suspect authorities had begun to design his specific ToJ since the 1000 Hells, at least.<br /> <br /> His name, Voormas, appeared in that book directly.<br /> <br /> Page 34, the silent stronghold of Tou Mu<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her honored guest, the chi\u2019n at Voormas, perhaps the greatest of Kali\u2019s children, resides here while he avoids the justice of those he betrayed. </div> </div> </div>I remember this very well, this is a BIG crossover, the name of an important plot npc DIRECTLY appears in another game line. And he is an in-game npc, not someone like Caine, Set, etc, who originally comes from \u201creality\u201d. Others I can recall now is hunter Driver300, who appears in Giovanni Rev, and hunter Wendell, who injured Lucifer permanently in ToJ intro novel. Of course, DtF is originally a source series of HtR.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1265809-fates-of-canon-npcs-experiencing-avatar-storm?p=1355330#post1355330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably classify the Jade Demon as a Wu Lung barrabus rather than Akashic. Though I suppose it doesn't matter much, as he was probably one of the Gall\u00fb for hundreds of years before the Gilledeans came along and he joined their number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, Akashic Brotherhood Rev. says he is the most famous Akashic archmage (Okay... they count a Nephandi as one of them), and maybe the oldest \u201cTradition\u201d mage (nearly 800-year-old, in BoC he is apparently a Song Dynasty mage.), and a Do master ( In BoC he has Mediation 6, of course the Do hadn\u2019t been released at that time, it first appeared in Book of Shadows)<br /> <br /> *I always think WW should publish the revised book of BoC and Book of Shadows (Players Guide). They are very good but old as pain. To me Book of Chantries is the MtA version of Children of the Night, having many great npcs and chantries (Dossietep!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 12-17-2019, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}